From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: wait for decoder drain and pending presentation at EOF

The compressed input queue can empty before the first native frame finishes.
Keep an epoch-owned drain request until the decoder reports actual EOF, rather
than closing a not-yet-synchronized video thread when message bytes reach zero.
The parent continues handling startup/resync and seek/abort messages.

Drain cooperatively on the video thread. Keep an OUTPUT_AGAIN picture until
accepted by the renderer and send its startup notification only once, including
after backpressure. Distinguish failed and canceled drains from real EOF; reset
and stream changes cannot complete a replacement epoch. Do not decode again
after terminal EOF while the renderer consumes its remaining presentations.

Keep the existing 40-second bound for synchronous CloseStream only. Natural
EOF waits on actual decoder and render state, not a timer or repeated input.

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDMessage.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDMessage.h
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 
